    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nbase16, hues\n\n### Description\n\n`@lsp.mod.defaultLibrary` is very aggressive, and the logic behind what it considers to be from defaultLibrary seems almost arbitrary. In [neovim/neovim#27929](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/27929), it was agreed not to highlight it. Perhaps we should follow suit for both modules with mini?\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/abd71465-1b3e-4626-bbf3-d57b4fa6a7d5)\r\n\r\nvs\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/779e91fe-7549-4121-b36a-1a4ad34ce66b)\r\n",
